<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gafsa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Capsa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gafsa is a city in west-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, built around an oasis at the edge of the desert. As Capsa it was a Numidian town taken by Marius in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurthine-war">Jugurthine War</a>, then a Roman town and a Byzantine stronghold; in the 6th century it was the centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antalas">Antalas</a>. It gives its name to the prehistoric Capsian culture and is today a centre of phosphate mining.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gafsa.jpg" alt="Gafsa" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thedudeson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gafsa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
